			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I look at marketing for React conferences/events and see big budgets pushing overly complex solutions to problems you probably don’t really have. Compare to something like <a href=\"https://hypermedia.systems/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">hypermedia.systems/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> that got dropped by their publisher because they didn’t think the market was big enough and so have to self-publish. Such a shame when it has potential for building much simpler systems.</p>",
